File No. 14X002
Collateral Assignment of Easement and Track Lease, Page 1
 COLLATERAL ASSIGNMENT OF
RAILROAD EASEMENT AND TRACK LEASE

This COLLATERAL ASSIGNMENT OF RAILROAD EASEMENT AND TRACK LEASE (this
“Assignment”) is made as of the _____ day of _______________, 2014, by the CITY OF CHEY-
ENNE, a Wyoming municipal corporation, whose principal office and mailing address is locat-
ed at 2101 O’Neil Avenue, Cheyenne, WY 82001 (the “City”), to WYOMING BUSINESS COUN-
CIL (the “Council”), a body corporate organized under the laws of the State of Wyoming and
operating as a state instrumentality operated solely for the public benefit, whose principal
office and mailing address is located at 214 West 15th Street, Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001.
A. City has made a loan to Granite Peak Development Limited Partnership, a Wyoming lim-
ited partnership formerly known as Granite Peak Development, LLC, a Wyoming Lim-
ited Liability Company (“Granite”), in the stated principal sum of $3,000,000 (the “Gran-
ite Loan”), as evidenced by a Non-Negotiable Promissory Note dated as of even date
herewith made by Granite and the City and guarantied by Rich Fairservis (the “Guaran-
tor”), all in connection with the project (the “Project”) to construct railways, spurs, and
switching and related facilities to serve the Swan Ranch Rail Park (the “Park”) in Chey-
enne, Wyoming.
B. During construction and afterward during the pendency of the Granite Loan, the City will
own the project improvements pursuant to an Assignment of Ownership of Rail, Ties,
and all Related Rail Equipment installed pursuant to Amended And Restated Project De-
velopment and Administration Agreement dated as of even date herewith.
C. Pursuant to a Rail Road Right of Way Easement made as of even date herewith and rec-
orded on ______________, 2014, in Book _____ at Page _____ among the Real Estate
Records of the County Clerk for Laramie County, Wyoming (the “Rail Easement Agree-
ment”), made by Swan Ranch, LLC, a Wyoming limited liability company (“Swan”), and
Clear Creek Land Company LLC, a Wyoming limited liability company (“Clear Creek”),
the City will be the owner, for a term of ten (10) years from the date hereof, of a non-
exclusive easement (the “Rail Easement”) for a rail road line and corridor in Parcels 2, 3,
and 4, as described and shown on Exhibits A, B, and C attached hereto and made a part
hereof by this reference, subject to the rights of Granite, Swan, CLH, LLC, a Wyoming
limited liability company (“CLH”), and any related entity to an exclusive option to ac-
quire the rail, ties, and all related rail equipment within the Easement and all of the City’s
right, title, and interest in the Rail Easement.
D. The City has entered into a Track Lease Agreement for Rail Facilities Within Swan
Ranch Rail Park, Cheyenne, Wyoming (the “Track Lease”), with CLH and Granite under
which CLH will lease the City's rail facilities within the Park to serve various business
enterprises now or to be located within the Park.
E. The City has applied for, and been approved by the Council for, a Wyoming Business
Ready Community-Business Committed Loan in the maximum principal sum of Three
Million Dollars ($3,000,000) (the “Loan”), which the Council will disburse to the City as
provided in a Business Ready Community – Business Committed Loan Agreement made
as of even date herewith by the City in favor of the Council (the “Loan Agreement”).
F. The Granite Note is secured, in part, by a Mortgage (the “Mortgage”) upon the lands de-
scribed on Schedule 1 to the Loan Agreement granted to the City by Swan and Clear
```

### Page 2 of 3

```text
File No. 14X002
Collateral Assignment of Easement and Track Lease, Page 2
Creek, which Mortgage was made as of even date herewith and recorded on
______________, 2014, in Book _____ at Page _____ among the Real Estate Records of
the County Clerk for Laramie County, Wyoming.
G. The City’s obligations to repay the Loan to the Council is evidenced by a Promissory
Note (the “Note”) of even date herewith made in the maximum principal sum of the
Loan.

NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the Council agreeing to fund the Loan and oth-
er good and valuable consideration, the receipt of which is hereby acknowledged, and as further
security for the performance of the Obligations (as defined in the Loan Agreement), the City
hereby grants, conveys, transfers, and assigns to the Council all right, title, and interest of the
City in and to the Easement, the Rail Easement Agreement, and the Track Lease and all of the
City’s right, title and interest in and to the real estate therein described, and benefits under, in and
to the Rail Easement Agreement and the Track Lease.

TO HAVE AND TO HOLD the same with all of the rights, privileges and appurtenances
thereunto belonging unto the Council, its successors and assigns until such time as the Obliga-
tions have been satisfied in full for the purpose of further and collaterally securing same (but not,
however, for the purposes of securing any other obligations to Council, whether now existing or
hereafter arising).

The City and the Council agree that the following terms and conditions shall govern this
Assignment:
1. City’s Rights until Default.  So long as no default shall exist under the Obligations, the City
shall have the right to exercise all of the City’s rights and benefits under, in and to the Ease-
ment, the Rail Easement Agreement, and the Track Lease.
2. Council’s Rights in Event of Default.
2.1. Immediately upon the occurrence of a default under the Obligations, and until such de-
fault shall have been cured, as hereinafter defined, the Council is hereby expressly and
irrevocably authorized to assume any or all of City’s rights with respect to the Easement,
the Rail Easement Agreement, and the Track Lease without further authorization, notice
or demand and without the commencement of any action.
2.2. The City hereby constitutes and appoints the Council irrevocably, and with full power of
substitution and revocation, the true and lawful attorney, for and in the name, place and
stead of the City, to exercise any and all rights and remedies of the City under the Ease-
ment, the Rail Easement Agreement, and the Track Lease.  The City hereby grants unto
said attorney full power and authority to do and perform each and every act whatsoever
requisite to be done with respect to the Easement, the Rail Easement Agreement, and the
Track Lease, as fully to all intents and purposes, as the City could do if personally pre-
sent, hereby ratifying and confirming all that said attorney shall lawfully do or cause to
be done by virtue hereof, provided, however, that any acts or omissions by the Council
after default shall be at the Council’s discretion and shall not be or become the basis for
any liability of the City.
2.3. Acceptance of this Assignment by the Council shall not constitute a satisfaction of all or
any part of the Obligations of the City.
```

